  "body": "<!--\r\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nAs discussed in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/3957 and https://github.com/w3c/page-visibility/issues/39. Also while editing this, I found out that we're already [running visibility change steps before firing pageshow](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsing-the-web.html#session-history-document-visibility-change-steps), so after this change we have up-to-date visibility when either pagehide or pageshow is fired.\r\n\r\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\r\n   *  Blink (https://github.com/w3c/page-visibility/issues/39#issuecomment-401484560)\r\n   *  Gecko (https://github.com/w3c/page-visibility/issues/39#issuecomment-389486782)\r\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\r\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/25667\r\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/master/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\r\n   * Chrome: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1130950\r\n   * Firefox: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1667012\r\n   * Safari: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=216917\r\n\r\ncc @philipwalton @domenic @smaug---- @yoavweiss\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\r\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\r\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\r\n\r\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\r\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\r\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\r\n    and remove what's below.\r\n-->\r\n***\r\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5928/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Las